This directory holds the OpenSSL that a normal (BUNDLED) driver build links against.
The driver is shipped as a source tarball that has to build without a network, so the
static archives live here rather than being downloaded.

Version: openssl-3.5.7 (same release the CUBRID server bundles)

lib/{libssl.a,libcrypto.a} and include/  -  Linux x86_64, built from
  https://github.com/CUBRID/3rdparty/raw/develop/openssl/openssl-3.5.7.tar.gz
  SHA256=a8c0d28a529ca480f9f36cf5792e2cd21984552a3c8e4aa11a24aa31aeac98e8

  $ ./config --prefix=<dir> --libdir=lib no-shared no-module no-docs no-tests
  $ make && make install_sw

  --libdir=lib is required: OpenSSL 3.x otherwise installs into <dir>/lib64 on
  linux-x86_64. The Windows archives are built the same way with VS2015 (v140).

To refresh these, rebuild with the command above and copy include/ and lib/*.a here.
A build finds them missing - a platform with no shipped binaries, or a working copy
that never ran this step - falls back to downloading and building OpenSSL itself.
